2026-11-06T02:58:53.7280447Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7289972Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7291045Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7293294Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7293585Z 
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7293837Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7294271Z 
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7294611Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7295214Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7295572Z 
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7295829Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7296295Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7296561Z 
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7296850Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7297544Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T02:58:53.7297759Z 
